<title>BELGIUM: Toyota to invest $24 mln in Belgian parts centre.</title>
<headline>Toyota to invest $24 mln in Belgian parts centre.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese car maker Toyota said in a statement on Friday it planned to invest around 850 billion Belgian francs ($24 million) in its Toyota European Parts Centre (TPCE) in Diest, Belgium.  </p>
<p>The money would be spent on expanding the floor area of TPCE to 67,700 square metres from 37,700 square metres.</p>
<p>It would bring the total investment of Toyota Motor Europe in Europe to some 8.3 billion francs, of which 7.6 billion in Belgium.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
